                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Chau, thanks for taking this up. I have a few requests inline."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 436,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please let's avoid unrelated whitespace changes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 436,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1359,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you please put this code above the C++ typecheck functions on line 1294"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1359,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1370,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "For consistency I think it would be nice to add the macro wrapper to take the address of `dst` and rename this function to `pldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size` (double-underscore)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1370,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "But `dst` will always be of `size_t` type, so caller has to specify the necessary function name to specify the extract type. What else should the wrapper do? typecheck for size_t?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1370,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, take the address, and do a typecheck for `size_t`. I'd like the behaviour match the existing `_extract()` macros. Otherwise we should call it `pldm_msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size_p()` (`p` for \"pointer\"). I'd rather not do the latter."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1370,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This can just be `pldm_msgbuf_extract()` - the type is defined by `value` and the call will be correctly dispatched thanks to the `_Generic()` macro."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "When these functions use `pldm_msgbuf_extract()`, it fails with the below msg unless I put them inside #ifndef __cplusplus. I think something is wrong.\n\n> error: \u2018_Generic\u2019 was not declared in this scope"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "`_Generic` is not specified by C++. If you're hitting that error you're trying to compile the translation unit including the header with a C++ compiler. That should never happen in the library implementation as it's all C, and for the tests, you should be testing these APIs in `tests/msgbuf_generic.c` (for this reason)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "```\n LIBPLDM_CC_ALWAYS_INLINE int\n pldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(struct pldm_msgbuf *ctx, size_t *dst)\n {\n\t uint8_t value;\n\t int rc;\n \n\t if (!dst) {\n\t\t return -EINVAL;\n\t }\n \n\t rc = pldm_msgbuf_extract(ctx, value);\n\t if (rc) {\n\t\t return rc;\n\t }\n \n\t static_assert(SIZE_MAX >= UINT8_MAX, \"Invalid promotion\");\n \n\t *dst = value;\n\t return 0;\n }\n \n#define pldm_msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(ctx, dst) \\\n\tpldm_msgbuf_extract_typecheck(size_t, pldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size, dst, ctx, &(dst))\n```\n\nWith the above code added to msgbuf.hs at line 1294, when the test/*.cpp files include this msgbuf.h, the `pldm_msgbuf_extract()` line will be expanded and _Generic exposed. That's why it fails with the error unless I put it inside #ifndef __cplusplus, or make it a macro function."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Ugh, yeah, okay. Obviously I didn't think that through enough! Sorry for the detour, leave it as you have it, though maybe add a comment about it so the question is answered for anyone wondering the same."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Would you prefer putting them inside #ifndef __cplusplus? Otherwise, it has to be placed at the end to be able to use the c++ `pldm_msgbuf_typecheck_*` APIs, contradicting to your [comment](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/79130/comment/ca84d8ff_f187dfee/), as it will be built in the .cpp test files."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "No, please let's avoid more `#ifdef`ery where we can. Just use the typed function name as you have in the existing code.\n\nBut perhaps we can drop the typecheck from the macros I suggested. They're only required for unaligned stores. I'm not yet aware of cases where we need that. Just define them to take the address of the `size_t` parameter\n\n```c\n#define pldm_msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(ctx, dst) \\\n    pldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(ctx, &(dst))\nLIBPLDM_CC_ALWAYS_INLINE int\npldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(struct pldm_msgbuf *ctx, size_t *dst)\n{\n...\n}\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1379,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Above this line, can you add:\n\n```\nstatic_assert(SIZE_MAX >= UINT8_MAX, \"Invalid promotion\");\n```\n\nAnd similarly for the other implementations"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/msgbuf.h",
                    "line": 1384,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
            "files": [
                {
