                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we add the wrapper macros?\n\nFor this case:\n\n```c\n#define pldm_msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(ctx, dst) \\\n    pldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(ctx, &(dst)) \nLIBPLDM_CC_ALWAYS_INLINE int\npldm__msgbuf_extract_uint8_to_size(struct pldm_msgbuf *ctx, size_t *dst)\n{\n...\n}\n```\n\nThat way the call sites look the same as for the other extractors (no need to take the address of the destination in the call-site code).\n\nI mentioned this in the comment on PS2, though I guess it got lost in some of the discussion.\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/79130/comment/84535728_50b5520e/"
                },
